  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) achieved the best performance so far (acc=0.650, F1=0.628), clearly outperforming pca_n2000 under identical settings (config_002: acc=0.591). This confirms that learned RNA encoders help, but we have not yet tested scgpt, the third available RNA encoder. Question: Does scgpt outperform scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder under the same multiprofile+avgpool conditions? Why this is the best next step: config_008 provides a clean, controlled comparison against config_005 (only the RNA encoder changes). Resolving which learned encoder is superior is a critical design decision that directly determines the baseline for all subsequent multimodal experiments. Testing multimodal fusion now with an unconfirmed RNA encoder risks confounding the fusion question with an encoder choice. This experiment reduces uncertainty on the most impactful single variable before committing budget to the larger multimodal search space."
}

